cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  mag — detector versus decision rule: patient-level aggregation in
  automated malaria microscopy
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  paper it was written for.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NOT REPORTED — supply the author list before release"
repository-code: "NOT REPORTED — supply the repository URL before release"
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
abstract: >-
  A re-analysis package that separates the detector checkpoint from the
  patient-level aggregation rule in automated malaria microscopy. It runs the
  released detectors over the released archive, applies fourteen aggregation
  rules to the same detections, and refuses to write any result that cannot be
  traced to that run: there is no synthetic generation, no default cache path,
  and no fallback that manufactures an input a stage cannot find.
keywords:
  - malaria
  - microscopy
  - reproducibility
  - diagnostic-ai
  - aggregation
  - patient-level
